  "lineage": "Hazarajat highland tradition of central Afghanistan built on the fretless two-string long-necked dambora lute, sustained orally by village and shrine singers and brought to recording through Dawood Sarkhosh and Sarwar Sarkhosh from the 1980s exile period onward, marked by strummed drone-plus-melody right-hand patterns, no fixed fretting, moderate duple pulse, and Hazaragi-dialect poetry of exile, love and mourning delivered in a nasal high-tessitura solo voice.",
